This experiment develops an end-to-end Agentic AI system that combines RAG, database tools, intelligent agent routing, and a Streamlit interface. The system accepts user questions and selects the appropriate approach, such as retrieving information from a knowledge base, accessing student data from a SQLite database, or using an LLM for general questions.

Technologies: Python, Ollama, Llama 3.2, SQLite, Scikit-learn, Streamlit

Workflow:
User Question
      ↓
Main AI Agent
      ↓
 ┌───────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┐
 ↓               ↓               ↓
RAG Agent      SQL Tool       LLM Agent
 ↓               ↓               ↓
Knowledge      SQLite       General Answer
Base           Database
 └───────────────┴───────────────┘
                  ↓
              Final Answer
                  ↓
             Streamlit UI
Objective:
To build a complete Agentic AI application by integrating RAG, tool use, database interaction, LLM reasoning, and deployment through a web interface into a single end-to-end system.
